<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · concept</p><h1 class="enc-title">Westminster system</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Westminster parliamentary model, Westminster model</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Westminster system is the model of parliamentary government developed in the United Kingdom, in which the executive is drawn from and accountable to an elected legislature. It includes a ceremonial head of state, a prime minister and cabinet, and an official opposition. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> profile notes that it was adopted by the self-governing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominion">dominions</a> and many former colonies, making it one of the empire's most enduring legacies.</p></div>
